{
    "background_story": "Noel was a brilliant but eccentric artist known for his extravagant and impractical creations. His passion project, a sprawling, avant-garde sculpture garden, had been years in the making. Despite the warnings from friends and family, Noel poured his life savings into the project, ignoring the fact that it was unlikely to ever turn a profit. The garden, with its intricate mazes and elaborate water features, was a testament to Noel's creativity, but it was also a financial sinkhole. As the costs mounted, Noel's friends and family worried that he was throwing his money away on a pipe dream. Yet, Noel couldn't be swayed, convinced that his art was worth the financial risk. His uneconomical endeavors may have left him struggling to make ends meet, but they also brought him a sense of purpose and fulfillment.",
